/E (The Iskander-M navigation system, however, reveals a markedly different picture. In the examined INS, the identified microelectronics are entirely foreign-made, with U.S.-origin components accounting for 78.1%. These are not confined to a single peripheral function: U.S. components perform critical functions in signal processing, data conversion, programmable logic, memory, communications, and power management.)
