/Title (Compared with loitering munitions, where the share of Chinese microelectronics has gradually increased and is now roughly on par with that of U.S.-made components, the Iskander-M presents a markedly different picture. According to the latest data published by DIU, only around a quarter of the 140 identified Russian companies manufactured Iskander-M components. Nearly half were produced by U.S. manufacturers, with components sourced from Switzerland, Belarus, Germany, Taiwan, and China.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 832 0 R
/Next 906 0 R
>>
